3. Shadow movement

You said move between shadows. Good.

That means each silhouette has:

* a light form — funny / useful / attractive
* a shadow form — distorted / weaponized / tragic

Example:

Silhouette	Light Form	Shadow Form
Treasure Animal	resourceful adventurer	hoarding tyrant
Pattern Addict	brilliant clue-hunter	paranoid fanatic
Bureaucratic Warlord	organizer	petty despot
Human Siren	charming diplomat	manipulative vampire
Hypercompetent Idiot	genius	brittle alien
Child Knife	truth teller	little sadist
Performance Beast	energizer	attention addict

That gives you state transitions.

A scene can be built around:

* pushing someone from light → shadow
* redeeming shadow → light
* pairing two shadows so they explode
* putting a shadow version in a context where it becomes useful

