7. Tracking map

If we were building a reusable “Pantheon cast board,” I’d track each character on axes.

Axes

* order ↔ chaos
* sincerity ↔ irony
* competence ↔ incompetence
* appetite ↔ restraint
* status-seeking ↔ truth-seeking
* mystic ↔ procedural
* local ↔ cosmic
* light ↔ shadow

Then every scene becomes partly a geometry problem.

Example:

* Pattern Addict = chaos / sincere / medium-high competence / truth-seeking / cosmic
* Bureaucratic Warlord = order / sincere / medium competence / status-seeking / procedural
* Holy Appetitive = chaos / sincere / low abstraction / appetite / local
* Auditor = order / dry irony / high competence / truth-seeking / procedural

That lets you design collision vectors instead of guessing.

